From 5a90cf7b7b4e4532228b20da91344e7b21787ca5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tasker <tasker@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:30:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/35] hw/audio: intel-hda-ace: the host gateways (the module
 table, audio forwarding, the extended DMA-position registers)

The firmware's module table: init instance (0), large-config set (4),
bind (5) and delete instance (11) are parsed as the IPC4 header lays them
out (module id and instance in the primary; the size in dwords, the
pipeline, the core and the domain in the init-instance extension; the
destination module and the queues in the bind extension; the block flags,
the parameter id and the size of a large config), kept by module id and
instance, and answered like the pipeline messages.  Of a module's
configuration the model reads only what the plan's 5.6 defines and the
gateways need: the base configuration's buffer sizes and input audio
format, and -- when the configuration is 21 words and up, the copier's
tail -- the output format of pin 0 and the gateway node id, whose index
is the stream tag minus one (0xff: no stream yet, the driver's
placeholder).

The host gateways of the plan's 5.9: while a pipeline is RUNNING and a
host-output copier in it names a stream that is running, each period
drains that stream through DMA exactly as the ROM consumer drains the
loader stream -- the descriptor list walked as intel_hda_xfer() walks
it, bounded by SPIB -- and writes the bytes into the host-input gateway
stream of the copier bound behind it (through the modules bound in
between, which change nothing: the pipeline is a wire).  A period is the
run of descriptors up to the next that interrupts on completion and
takes as long as its bytes at the stream's rate, so the positions (LPIB,
the position buffer, and the vendor-specific extended DMA-position
registers at BAR0 + 0x1084, read-only, a mirror of the position buffer)
and the stream interrupts advance as the host expects.  Per period one
evidence line is traced for each stream: ace_audio <tag> <bytes> rms <r>
peak <p> first <s0> ... <s7>.

The wire, the pacing, a capture stream that is not running losing its
period, a frame that changes across the pipeline not being forwarded and
the table's answers the plan does not fix are model values.  The boot
path is unchanged: the ace_* trace of the 14 existing qtest cases is
that of 5680026's, case for case.
